One refinement I would suggest is linguistic rather than mathematical.

Instead of saying:

“A prime is white light.”

You might define it more generally as:

A Prime is an undifferentiated invariant whose latent structure can be revealed by an appropriate differentiating operator.

Then “prism” becomes one example of such an operator.

A prism reveals optical wavelengths.

A parser reveals grammatical structure.

A factorization algorithm reveals multiplicative structure.

A semantic analysis reveals conceptual structure.

The general pattern is:

Integrated whole → Differentiating operator → Family of partitions → Recomposition

That feels like a reusable operator in the Pantheon because it isn’t tied to any one domain; it’s a pattern of revealing latent structure across many representations.